---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import ScoreHistory from '../../components/ScoreHistory.astro';
import SharedResults from '../../components/SharedResults.astro';
import SebqInterpretation from '../../components/interpretation/SelfEvaluationOfBreathing.astro';
import { FAQ, FAQ_ORDER } from '../../tools/self-evaluation-of-breathing-questionnaire.content';
import { toolJsonLd } from '../../tools/jsonld';

const options = [
	{ short: 'Never / not true at all', value: 0 },
	{ short: 'Occasionally / a bit true', value: 1 },
	{ short: 'Frequently / mostly true', value: 2 },
	{ short: 'Very frequently / very true', value: 3 },
];

const items = [
	'I get easily breathless out of proportion to my fitness',
	'I notice myself breathing shallowly',
	'I get short of breath reading and talking',
	'I notice myself sighing',
	'I notice myself yawning',
	'I feel I cannot get a deep or satisfying breath',
	'I notice that I am breathing irregularly',
	'My breathing feels stuck or restricted',
	'My ribcage feels tight and cannot expand',
	'I notice myself breathing quickly',
	'I get breathless when I\'m anxious',
	'I find myself holding my breath',
	'I feel breathless in association with other physical symptoms',
	'I have trouble coordinating my breathing when I am speaking',
	'I can\'t catch my breath',
	'I feel that the air is stuffy, as if not enough air in the room',
	'I get breathless even when I am resting',
	'My breath feels like it does not go in all the way',
	'My breath feels like it does not go out all the way',
	'My breathing is heavy',
	'I feel that I am breathing more',
	'My breathing requires work',
	'My breathing requires effort',
	'I find myself breathing through my mouth during the day',
	'I breathe through my mouth at night while I sleep',
];

const pages = [items.slice(0, 13), items.slice(13)];

const jsonLd = toolJsonLd('Self-Evaluation of Breathing Questionnaire', '/tools/self-evaluation-of-breathing-questionnaire/', FAQ_ORDER.map(k => FAQ[k]));
---

<Page
	title="Self-Evaluation of Breathing Questionnaire (SEBQ): free online breathing pattern disorder questionnaire"
	description="Complete the 25-item Self-Evaluation of Breathing Questionnaire and get your SEBQ score out of 75 instantly, with the proposed threshold of 25 and reference values explained. The companion to the Nijmegen questionnaire for breathing pattern disorder. Free, no sign-up."
>
	<Fragment slot="head">
		<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)} />
	</Fragment>
			<div class="tool-header">
				<a href="/tools" class="section-label tools">Tools</a>
				<h1>Self-Evaluation of Breathing Questionnaire (SEBQ)</h1>
				<p class="subtitle">25 statements about how your breathing feels: the breathing-specific companion to the Nijmegen questionnaire</p>
				<p class="description">
					The Self-Evaluation of Breathing Questionnaire was developed by osteopath and breathing researcher Rosalba Courtney with Kenneth Greenwood and first published in 2009 as a 17-item version; the 25-item version here is the one used in later studies. <!-- REVIEW: header copy corrected against sources --> Where the <a href="/tools/nijmegen/">Nijmegen questionnaire</a> was written for hyperventilation and includes tingling, palpitations, and anxiety, the SEBQ asks only about breathing: whether it feels shallow, restricted, effortful, irregular, or unsatisfying. That makes it better at picking up the sense of restricted, effortful breathing, which the Nijmegen largely misses.
				</p>
				<p class="description">
					You rate each of 25 statements from <strong>0 (never / not true at all)</strong> to <strong>3 (very frequently / very true)</strong>, for a total of 0–75. The 2016 reliability study by Mitchell and colleagues found the questionnaire very consistent over two weeks (ICC 0.89) and an average score of about 15 among the 180 people who took part. No validated cut-off exists: a score of <strong>25 or more</strong> has been used in research on expert opinion, but it has not been checked against a diagnosis.
				</p>
				<p class="description">
					The questionnaire is presented in two pages of 12–13 statements and takes about five minutes. If you have not done the <a href="/tools/nijmegen/">Nijmegen questionnaire</a>, the two together give a fuller picture: the Nijmegen for the systemic symptoms of over-breathing, the SEBQ for the breathing sensations themselves.
				</p>
				<div class="disclaimer">
					<strong>This is not a diagnostic tool.</strong> Breathlessness has many causes, including cardiac and lung disease that need investigation in their own right. A high SEBQ score suggests that assessment of breathing pattern by a respiratory physiotherapist may be worthwhile; it does not establish a diagnosis of breathing pattern disorder or exclude anything else. Discuss your results with your doctor. Based on: Courtney R, Greenwood KM. <em>Preliminary investigation of a measure of dysfunctional breathing symptoms: the Self Evaluation of Breathing Questionnaire (SEBQ).</em> Int J Osteopath Med. 2009;12(4):121–127; and Mitchell AJ, Bacon CJ, Moran RW. <em>Reliability and determinants of Self-Evaluation of Breathing Questionnaire (SEBQ) score.</em> Appl Psychophysiol Biofeedback. 2016;41(1):111–120. The questionnaire is the work of its authors; this page is an interactive scoring aid for personal, non-commercial use.
				</div>
			</div>

			<form id="sebq-form" novalidate>
				<div class="progress-wrap">
					<div class="progress-text"><span id="progress-label">Page 1 of 2</span></div>
					<div class="progress-bar"><div id="progress-fill" class="progress-fill"></div></div>
				</div>
				<p class="form-instructions">For each statement, choose how often it applies to you, or how true it is of your breathing, as things generally are for you at the moment.</p>

				{pages.map((page, p) => (
					<section class="step" data-step={p} hidden={p > 0}>
						{page.map((text, i) => {
							const n = p === 0 ? i + 1 : i + 14;
							return (
								<div class="symptom" data-id={`i${n}`}>
									<p class="symptom-text"><span class="num">{n}.</span> {text}</p>
									<div class="segmented">
										{options.map(opt => (
											<label><input type="radio" name={`i${n}`} value={opt.value} /><span>{opt.short}</span></label>
										))}
									</div>
								</div>
							);
						})}
						<div class="step-footer">
							{p > 0 ? <button type="button" class="back-step-btn" data-prev>← Back</button> : <span></span>}
							{p === pages.length - 1
								? <button type="submit" class="submit-btn">Calculate my score</button>
								: <button type="button" class="next-btn" data-next>Next page →</button>}
						</div>
					</section>
				))}
			</form>

			<div id="results" class="results" hidden>
				<h2>Your SEBQ score</h2>
				<div class="total-score">
					<span id="total-score-value">—</span>
					<span class="total-score-label">out of 75</span>
				</div>
				<p id="score-interpretation" class="score-interp"></p>

				<h3>Your highest-rated statements</h3>
				<div id="chart" class="chart"></div>

				<ScoreHistory toolId="self-evaluation-of-breathing-questionnaire" toolName="SEBQ" />

				<button type="button" id="back-btn" class="back-btn">Edit answers</button>
			</div>

			<SharedResults toolId="self-evaluation-of-breathing-questionnaire" />

			<SebqInterpretation />
</Page>

<script>
import { trackStep } from '../../scripts/pageview';
import { selfEvaluationOfBreathingQuestionnaire } from '../../tools/self-evaluation-of-breathing-questionnaire';
import { interpretResult } from '../../scripts/results/interpretation';
import { mountScoreHistory, mountSharedResults } from '../../scripts/results/scoreHistory';

const N = 25;
const form = document.getElementById('sebq-form') as HTMLFormElement;
const steps = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.step'));
const progressLabel = document.getElementById('progress-label') as HTMLElement;
const progressFill = document.getElementById('progress-fill') as HTMLElement;
const results = document.getElementById('results') as HTMLElement;
let currentStep = 0;

const history = mountScoreHistory(selfEvaluationOfBreathingQuestionnaire);
mountSharedResults(selfEvaluationOfBreathingQuestionnaire);

function getVal(n: number): number | null {
	const checked = form.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>(`input[name="i${n}"]:checked`);
	return checked ? parseInt(checked.value, 10) : null;
}
function itemText(n: number): string {
	const el = form.querySelector<HTMLElement>(`.symptom[data-id="i${n}"] .symptom-text`);
	return (el?.textContent || '').replace(/^\s*\d+\.\s*/, '').trim();
}
function flag(n: number) {
	const el = form.querySelector<HTMLElement>(`.symptom[data-id="i${n}"]`);
	el?.classList.add('missing');
	el?.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'center' });
	setTimeout(() => el?.classList.remove('missing'), 2500);
}
function showStep(n: number) {
	currentStep = Math.max(0, Math.min(n, steps.length - 1));
	steps.forEach(s => { s.hidden = parseInt(s.dataset.step || '0', 10) !== currentStep; });
	progressLabel.textContent = `Page ${currentStep + 1} of ${steps.length}`;
	progressFill.style.width = `${((currentStep + 1) / (steps.length + 1)) * 100}%`;
	window.scrollTo({ top: (form.getBoundingClientRect().top + window.scrollY) - 20, behavior: 'smooth' });
	if (currentStep > 0) trackStep(currentStep + 1, `Page ${currentStep + 1}`);
}
function validateStep(n: number): boolean {
	const range = n === 0 ? [1, 13] : [14, 25];
	for (let i = range[0]; i <= range[1]; i++) {
		if (getVal(i) === null) { flag(i); return false; }
	}
	return true;
}
form.querySelectorAll('[data-next]').forEach(btn => btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
	if (!validateStep(currentStep)) return;
	showStep(currentStep + 1);
}));
form.querySelectorAll('[data-prev]').forEach(btn => btn.addEventListener('click', () => showStep(currentStep - 1)));

form.addEventListener('submit', (e) => {
	e.preventDefault();
	if (!validateStep(currentStep)) return;
	const vals: { n: number; v: number }[] = [];
	for (let i = 1; i <= N; i++) vals.push({ n: i, v: getVal(i)! });
	const total = vals.reduce((s, x) => s + x.v, 0);
	(document.getElementById('total-score-value') as HTMLElement).textContent = String(total);

	// REVIEW: Layer 1 copy. No validated cut-off or bands (see the content
	// module), so the config has none and interpretResult adds nothing yet.
	const subscores = Object.fromEntries(vals.map(x => [`i${x.n}`, x.v]));
	const opening = `Your SEBQ score is ${total} out of 75; in a 2016 study of 180 people the average was 15.1.`;
	const context = total >= 25
		? 'Your score is at or above 25, a point suggested by expert opinion but never validated, so treat it as a reason to ask about a breathing assessment rather than a result in itself.'
		: 'There is no validated cut-off, so the statements you rated highest, below, say more than the total about which sensations bother you.';
	(document.getElementById('score-interpretation') as HTMLElement).textContent =
		[opening, interpretResult(selfEvaluationOfBreathingQuestionnaire, { total, subscores }, history.latest()), context].filter(Boolean).join(' ');

	const top = vals.filter(x => x.v > 0).sort((a, b) => b.v - a.v || a.n - b.n).slice(0, 8);
	(document.getElementById('chart') as HTMLElement).innerHTML = top.length ? top.map(x => `
		<div class="chart-row">
			<div class="chart-label">${x.n}. ${itemText(x.n)}</div>
			<div class="chart-track"><div class="chart-bar" style="width:${Math.max(2, Math.round((x.v / 3) * 100))}%"></div></div>
			<div class="chart-val">${x.v}</div>
		</div>`).join('') : '<p class="none">You rated every statement 0.</p>';

	form.hidden = true;
	results.hidden = false;
	history.record({ total, subscores });
	results.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
	trackStep('results', 'Results');
});

document.getElementById('back-btn')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
	results.hidden = true;
	form.hidden = false;
	showStep(0);
});
</script>

<style>
	.tool-header { padding-bottom: 1.5em; border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light)); margin-bottom: 2em; }
	.tool-header h1 { margin: 0.3em 0 0.1em; }
	.subtitle { color: rgb(var(--gray)); font-size: 1.05em; margin: 0 0 0.75em; }
	.description { margin-bottom: 1em; }

	.progress-wrap { margin-bottom: 1.25em; }
	.progress-text { font-size: 0.82em; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.04em; text-transform: uppercase; color: rgb(var(--gray)); margin-bottom: 0.4em; }
	.progress-bar { height: 7px; background: rgb(var(--gray-light)); border-radius: 4px; overflow: hidden; }
	.progress-fill { height: 100%; background: var(--accent); border-radius: 4px; transition: width 0.3s ease; width: 33%; }

	.form-instructions { font-size: 0.88em; color: rgb(var(--gray-dark)); background: var(--accent-light); border-radius: 6px; padding: 0.7em 1.1em; margin-bottom: 1.25em; }

	.symptom { border: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light)); border-radius: 8px; padding: 0.9em 1.2em; margin-bottom: 0.65em; transition: border-color 0.15s, box-shadow 0.15s; }
	.symptom.missing { border-color: #c0392b; box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(192, 57, 43, 0.12); }
	.symptom-text { margin: 0 0 0.7em; font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.95em; line-height: 1.4; }
	.num { color: rgb(var(--gray)); margin-right: 0.3em; }

	.segmented { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: 0.3em; max-width: 40em; }
	.segmented label { position: relative; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; text-align: center; font-size: 0.82em; padding: 0.5em 0.4em; border: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light)); border-radius: 5px; cursor: pointer; transition: background 0.1s, border-color 0.1s; line-height: 1.25; }
	.segmented label:hover { border-color: var(--accent); }
	.segmented input { position: absolute; opacity: 0; width: 0; height: 0; }
	.segmented label:has(input:checked) { background: var(--accent-light); border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--accent-dark); font-weight: 700; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--accent); }

	.step-footer { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 1em; padding: 1.5em 0 0.5em; }
	.next-btn, .submit-btn { background: var(--accent); color: #fff; border: none; padding: 0.75em 1.6em; border-radius: 5px; font-size: 1em; font-weight: 700; cursor: pointer; font-family: inherit; }
	.next-btn:hover, .submit-btn:hover { background: var(--accent-dark); }
	.back-step-btn, .back-btn { background: none; border: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light)); padding: 0.75em 1.25em; border-radius: 5px; font-size: 0.95em; cursor: pointer; color: rgb(var(--gray)); font-family: inherit; }
	.back-step-btn:hover, .back-btn:hover { border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--accent); }

	.results { padding-top: 1em; }
	.results h2 { margin-bottom: 0.5em; }
	.results h3 { margin-top: 1.75em; margin-bottom: 0.4em; }
	.total-score { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.5em; margin: 1em 0; }
	#total-score-value { font-size: 3.5em; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent); line-height: 1; }
	.total-score-label { color: rgb(var(--gray)); font-size: 1.1em; }
	.score-interp { font-size: 1em; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0 0 1em; padding: 1em 1.25em; background: var(--accent-light); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 4px; }

	.chart { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5em; margin: 1em 0; }
	.chart :global(.chart-row) { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 20em 1fr 2em; align-items: center; gap: 0.75em; font-size: 0.88em; }
	.chart :global(.chart-label) { text-align: right; color: rgb(var(--gray-dark)); line-height: 1.25; }
	.chart :global(.chart-track) { background: rgb(var(--gray-light)); border-radius: 4px; height: 1.5em; overflow: hidden; }
	.chart :global(.chart-bar) { height: 100%; background: var(--accent); border-radius: 4px; min-width: 2px; transition: width 0.4s ease; }
	.chart :global(.chart-val) { font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent); text-align: right; }
	.chart :global(.none) { color: rgb(var(--gray)); }

	.back-btn { margin-top: 1.5em; }

	@media (max-width: 640px) {
		.symptom { padding: 0.8em 0.9em; }
		.segmented { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); max-width: none; }
		.chart :global(.chart-row) { grid-template-columns: 10em 1fr 1.6em; gap: 0.5em; font-size: 0.8em; }
	}
</style>
